{
  "_comment": "Data for scripts/frontend_scaffolder.py. 'structure' maps paths to content keys; 'contents' maps content keys to files under this folder; 'configs', 'package' and each feature are per template; keys in 'use_client' get a 'use client' directive in the nextjs template.",
  "_pins": "Checked on npm 2026-11-08. typescript stays on 6.0.x (~6.0.0), not 7: typescript-eslint 8.72 (used by both lint setups, inside eslint-config-next too) declares typescript >=4.8.4 <6.1.0. Next keeps eslint ^9: eslint-config-next 16.4 bundles eslint-plugin-react 7.37, eslint-plugin-import 2.32 and eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y 6.10, whose peer ranges stop at eslint 9. The Vite config uses only @eslint/js, typescript-eslint and eslint-plugin-react-hooks 7, which all accept eslint 10. @types/node ^24 in both templates matches create-vite's react-ts template.",
  "name_placeholder": "__PROJECT_NAME__",
